WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.363
Hi, I'm Radar!

00:00:02.363 --> 00:00:05.939
Needle 3, a tiny tool-calling model, scores its own calls.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.800
Here's how, and why local fine-tuning loses it.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.473
A small post-hoc head reads the whole network, prompt and finished call

00:00:14.473 --> 00:00:16.535
together, and judges the call afterwards.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:22.762
The head reads the prompt and call at all twenty-one depths: the

00:00:22.762 --> 00:00:24.830
embedding, plus each of the twenty blocks.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.723
Eighty-four probe vectors, one per depth and lane, each pool the

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:29.986
trace into a summary.

00:00:30.407 --> 00:00:34.782
Four query vectors attend across those summaries, then project down to one logit.

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:39.238
Confidence is the lower of that score and the decoder's own probability.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.584
Both have to agree.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.451
The head reads the backbone under stop gradient.

00:00:44.451 --> 00:00:47.614
Training it cannot move one weight of the model it judges.

00:00:48.034 --> 00:00:51.300
It was trained in a separate run and merged in afterwards.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.785
No gradient path reaches it.

00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:57.397
A local LoRA moves accuracy eighteen to thirty-six points, so the old

00:00:57.397 --> 00:01:00.191
head would predict failures that no longer happen.

00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:03.893
So the build deletes the head, and confidence comes back as None.

00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:09.930
Cactus's own chart, on Mobile Actions: grey is the base, orange the fine-tune.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.331
The two-layer slice goes from zero point nine to sixty-six point seven.

00:01:14.751 --> 00:01:17.600
At twenty layers, the tuned bar sits below the base.

00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:23.839
The local path also exports at four bits: its packer refuses anything else.

00:01:23.839 --> 00:01:29.087
A tuned archive is sixty-three point four four megabytes, not thirty-five point three four.

00:01:30.558 --> 00:01:33.192
Calibration is a fit, and a fit needs samples.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:36.412
The head must be retrained with the model, on your tools.

00:01:39.275 --> 00:01:43.106
A detached probe judges each call; a local fine-tune drops it and

00:01:43.106 --> 00:01:44.383
exports at four bits.

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:46.904
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.904 --> 00:01:47.504
I'm Radar.

00:01:47.504 --> 00:01:47.804
Bye!
